            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Gujarati for pair, then the Gujarati for to test."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ચૂકવવું",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ચૂકવવું — cūkavvũ — \"to pay, to settle\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "હું દુકાનદારને પૈસા ચૂકવું છું. — hũ dukāndārne paisā cūkavũ chũ — \"I pay the shopkeeper the money.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ચૂકવવું (cūkavvũ) is a tadbhava, the causative of a verb built on cukk, \"fall short of, stop\", a reconstructed form. CDIAL glosses the Gujarati word \"to discharge, settle\" (CDIAL 4848)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for everyday life at A2."
